// ATT&CK: execution, persistence, privilege-escalation, stealth, T1574
// Description: Detects the persistent configuration of a .NET startup hook through the "DOTNET_STARTUP_HOOKS"
//   environment variable. An assembly configured in this variable is loaded and executed before the
//   entry point of every affected .NET application.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate observability, profiling, or development tooling that configures a .NET startup hook persistently
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/tools/dotnet-environment-variables#dotnet_startup_hooks
//   - https://persistence-info.github.io/Data/dotnetstartuphooks.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/dbf1325c93b98449a11d7eee64254da52dfdec2e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_dotnet_startup_hooks.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\DOTNET_STARTUP_HOOKS"
